"note\": \"Degraded throughput while a stuck job retried; killed job and drained queue.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nNewest first: 11-09, 11-07, 10-28, 10-14.\n\nsrc/incidents.ts:\n\n```ts\nimport { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n\nexport type IncidentSeverity = \"minor\" | \"major\";\n\nexport interface Incident {\n  // ISO timestamp of when the incident was logged.\n  time: string;\n  service: string;\n  severity: IncidentSeverity;\n  note: string;\n}\n\nconst SEVERITIES: IncidentSeverity[] = [\"minor\", \"major\"];\n\nexport function loadIncidents(path = new URL(\"../data/incidents.json\", import.meta.url)): Incident[] {\n  const data = JSON.parse(readFileSync(path, \"utf8\")) as Incident[];\n  for (const inc of data) {\n    if (!SEVERITIES.includes(inc.severity)) throw new Error(`${inc.service}: unknown severity ${inc.severity}`);\n    if (Number.isNaN(Date.parse(inc.time))) throw new Error(`${inc.service}: bad time ${inc.time}`);\n  }\n  return newestFirst(data);\n}\n\n// Descending by time, stable for ties.\nexport function newestFirst(incidents: Incident[]): Incident[] {\n  return [...incidents].sort((a, b) => Date.parse(b.time) - Date.parse(a.time));\n}\n```\n\nChanges to app.ts:\n\n```ts\nimport { loadStatus, type StatusData } from \"./services.ts\";\nimport { loadIncidents, type Incident } from \"./incidents.ts\";\nimport { renderPage } from \"./render.ts\";\n\nexport function createApp(status: StatusData = loadStatus(), incidents: Incident[] = loadIncidents()) {\n  const app = express();\n  app.use(express.static(...));\n  app.get(\"/\", (_req, res) => res.type(\"html\").send(renderPage(status, incidents)));\n  app.get(\"/api/status\", (_req, res) => res.json(status));\n  app.get(\"/api/incidents\", (_req, res) => res.json(incidents));\n  return app;\n}\n```\n\nrender.ts: add `renderIncidents(incidents: Incident[]): string` and a section.\n\n```ts\nconst SEVERITY_LABEL = { minor: \"Minor\", major: \"Major\" };\n\nfunction utcTime(iso: string): string {\n  return new Date(iso).toLocaleString(\"en-GB\", {\n    day: \"numeric\", month: \"short\", hour: \"2-digit\", minute: \"2-digit\", timeZone: \"UTC\",\n  });\n}\n```\n\nActually, `updated` in renderPage does this inline; extract it into a shared helper and use it for both.\n\nrenderIncident:\n\n```ts\nfunction renderIncident(inc: Incident): string {\n  return `\n        <li class=\"incident ${inc.severity}\">\n          <span class=\"incident-time\"><time datetime=\"${inc.time}\">${utcTime(inc.time)}</time></span>\n          <span class=\"incident-meta\"><span class=\"incident-sev\">${SEVERITY_LABEL[inc.severity]}</span> · <span class=\"incident-service\">${escapeHtml(inc.service)}</span></span>\n          <p class=\"incident-note\">${escapeHtml(inc.note)}</p>\n        </li>`;\n}\n```\n\nHmm, simpler structure:\n\n```html\n<section aria-label=\"Incident history\">\n  <h2>Incident history</h2>\n  <ol class=\"timeline\">\n    <li class=\"incident major\">\n      <div class=\"incident-head\">\n        <span class=\"incident-service\">worker</span>\n        <time datetime=\"2026-11-09T13:55:00Z\">9 Nov 13:55 UTC</time>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"incident-note\">...</p>\n      <span class=\"incident-sev major\">Major</span>?\n    </li>\n  </ol>\n</section>\n```\n\nDesign: timeline with left-border colored by severity, dot marker. Keep the existing aesthetic: card with border-radius 14px, same as services. Each incident: small monospace service name, muted time, severity badge, note.\n\nLet's go with this:\n\n```html\n<section aria-label=\"Incident history\">\n  <h2 class=\"section-title\">Incident history</h2>\n  <ol class=\"timeline\">\n    <li class=\"incident major\">\n      <div class=\"incident-head\">\n        <span class=\"incident-service\">worker</span>\n        <span class=\"incident-sev\">Major</span>\n        <time class=\"incident-time\" datetime=\"...\">9 Nov 13:55 UTC</time>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"incident-note\">...</p>\n    </li>\n    ...\n  </ol>\n</section>\n```\n\nCSS:\n\n```css\n.section-title {\n  margin: 28px 0 0;\n  font: 600 14px/1.3 -apple-system, ...;\n}\n```\n\nActually, services have no title; add \"Incident history\" as a heading. Use the same font as h2? Service h2 is monospace 16px. Section title: make it a similar eyebrow? Simplest:\n\n```css\n.section-title {\n  margin: 32px 0 10px;\n  font-size: 13px;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  letter-spacing: 0.06em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: var(--muted);\n}\n```\n\nThis matches the eyebrow style. Good.\n\n```css\n.timeline {\n  list-style: none;\n  margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n  background: var(--card);\n  border: 1px solid var(--line);\n  border-radius: 14px;\n}\n.incident { padding: 14px 16px; border-left: 3px solid var(--down); }\n.incident + .incident { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }\n.incident.minor { border-left-color: var(--degraded); }\n.incident.major { border-left-color: var(--down); }\n\n.incident-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }\n.incident-service { font: 600 14px/1.3 ui-monospace, \"SF Mono\", Menlo, monospace; }\n.incident-sev {\n  padding: 2px 8px;\n  border-radius: 999px;\n  font-size: 11px;\n  font-weight: 600;\n}\n.incident.minor .incident-sev { background: var(--degraded-soft); color: #9a6a00; }\n.incident.major .incident-sev { background: var(--down-soft); color: #b42323; }\n.incident-time { margin-left: auto; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); }\n.incident-note { margin: 6px 0 0; font-size: 13px; }\n```\n\n\"Color coded by severity\" — the left border + badge covers it.\n\nTests:\n\ntest/incidents.test.ts:\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, expect, it } from \"vitest\";\nimport { loadIncidents, newestFirst, type Incident } from \"../src/incidents.ts\";\nimport { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { mkdtempSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { tmpdir } from \"node:os\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\n```\n\nHmm, the existing test files don't write temp files. To test loadIncidents with a temp file: use fs.mkdtempSync(os.tmpdir()). Or test validation by writing a bad file. Let me write:\n\n```ts\nimport { mkdtempSync, writeFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { tmpdir } from \"node:os\";\nimport { join } from \"node:path\";\nimport { describe, expect, it } from \"vitest\";\nimport { loadIncidents, newestFirst, type Incident } from \"../src/incidents.ts\";\n\nfunction writeIncidents(incidents: unknown): string {\n  const dir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), \"incidents-\"));\n  const path = join(dir, \"incidents.json\");\n  writeFileSync(path, JSON.stringify(incidents));\n  return path;\n}\n\ndescribe(\"loadIncidents\", () => {\n  it(\"reads the data file and orders newest first\", () => {\n    const incidents = loadIncidents();\n    expect(incidents.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n    const times = incidents.map((i) => Date.parse(i.time));\n    expect(times).toEqual([...times].sort((a, b) => b - a));\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws on an unknown severity\", () => {\n    const path = writeIncidents([{ time: \"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\", service: \"api\", severity: \"weird\", note: \"x\" }]);\n    expect(() => loadIncidents(path)).toThrow(/severity/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws on an unparseable time\", () => {\n    const path = writeIncidents([{ time: \"nope\", service: \"api\", severity: \"minor\", note: \"x\" }]);\n    expect(() => loadIncidents(path)).toThrow(/time/);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"newestFirst\", () => {\n  it(\"sorts descending, keeping ties stable\", () => {\n    const mk = (t: string, n: string): Incident => ({ time: t, service: \"s\", severity: \"minor\", note: n });\n    expect(newestFirst([mk(\"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\", \"a\"), mk(\"2026-03-01T00:00:00Z\", \"b\"), mk(\"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\", \"c\")]).map(i => i.note)).toEqual([\"b\", \"a\", \"c\"]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\nNote: `loadIncidents(path)` — path is a string; the default parameter is a URL. readFileSync accepts both string | URL. The type should be `string | URL`. In services.ts the parameter is typed as `new URL(...)` which is URL. Let me type it as `path: string | URL = new URL(...)`.\n\nAlso add tests to app.test.ts:\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"incident timeline\", () => {\n  it(\"renders incidents newest first, coloured by severity\", async () => {\n    const res = await request(createApp()).get(\"/\");\n    const incidents = loadIncidents();\n    const times = incidents.map((i) => i.time);\n    let last = times.length;\n    for (const t of times) {\n      const idx = res.text.indexOf(`datetime=\"${t}\"`);\n      expect(idx).toBeGreaterThan(-1);\n      expect(idx).toBeLessThan(last);\n      last = idx;\n    }\n  });\n\n  it(\"shows severity badges and notes\", async () => {\n    const res = await request(createApp()).get(\"/\");\n    for (const inc of loadIncidents()) {\n      expect(res.text).toContain(escapeHtml(inc.note)); // hmm, note might contain characters\n    }\n  });\n});\n```\n\nNote: the `datetime=` attribute appears on the <time> element. The notes are plain text — contain `~40 min`. That's fine, escapeHtml is the identity here.\n\nSimpler: check the number of `class=\"incident` occurrences = incidents.length; check the ordering via the position of the datetime attributes; check severity classes: `li class=\"incident major\"` etc.\n\nAlso a `/api/incidents` test: `expect(res.body).toEqual(loadIncidents())`.\n\nNow, the existing test `expect(res.body).toEqual(loadStatus())` — no changes, good.\n\nrenderPage signature: `renderPage(data: StatusData, incidents: Incident[])`. render.ts imports the Incident type from incidents.ts.\n\nExtract a shared time-formatting helper:\n\n```ts\nfunction formatUtc(iso: string): string {\n  return new Date(iso).toLocaleString(\"en-GB\", {\n    day: \"numeric\", month: \"short\", hour: \"2-digit\", minute: \"2-digit\", timeZone: \"UTC\",\n  });\n}\n```\n\nUse in renderPage for `updated`, and in renderIncident for the time.\n\nAlso tsconfig — check if it's strict. Probably fine.\n\nEdge case: severity union type for SEVERITIES.includes — same pattern as services.ts, no problem.\n\nLet me quickly check tsconfig? Strict mode might complain about `JSON.parse as Incident[]`. services.ts does the same thing. OK.\n\nNow let's write the files.\n"},"turnId":"turn-msg_1c098fc65001qgMZbDNnPZwXXi"}],"kind":"items","sessionId":"s_b4zhctffop","ts":"2026-11-09T08:59:23.601576-05:00"}}
